<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Scoti</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Scotti</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Scoti was the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> name for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaels">Gaels</a> of Ireland, first used by Roman writers in the fourth century, when they raided Roman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>. Some settled in western Britain, and Gaels from Ireland and the kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dal-riata">Dál Riata</a> spread their language across northern Britain. The name passed to them there, and from it comes the name <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/scoti.jpg" alt="Scoti" width="320" height="419" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Charles Colbeck Edited by Yarl · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Public_Schools_Historical_Atlas_-_Roman_Britain_400.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
